{% extends 'layout.njk' %}
{% block content %}
<section class="intro intro-revised" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
  <div class="intro-main">
    <p class="intro-kicker">Wireless systems · Machine learning</p>
    <h1 id="intro-title">When should a phone change cells?</h1>
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <p>I’m an electronics and communication engineering graduate exploring how machine learning can help wireless networks make better decisions as people move. A handover can improve a connection, but frequent switching can also disrupt it.</p>
      <p>My first-author study applies graph-based reinforcement learning to this problem and was accepted for presentation at the <strong>19th IOE Graduate Conference (2026)</strong>. It grew from our one-year final project; I worked collaboratively on implementation, evaluation, validation, analysis, and manuscript revision.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-actions" role="group" aria-label="Research and CV">
      <a class="primary-link" href="/research/">Read the research</a>
      <a href="/assets/documents/Saange_Tamang_Academic_CV.pdf">Academic CV (PDF)</a>
    </div>
    <p class="availability">Seeking funded master’s or PhD research opportunities for Fall 2027.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section featured-research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2><a href="/research/">Full study and supporting material</a></div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <h3 class="publication-title"><a href="/research/">{{ profile.paperTitle }}</a></h3>
    <p class="authors"><strong>Saange Tamang</strong>, Sulav Kandel</p>
    <p class="status">{{ profile.paperStatus }}</p>
    <p class="research-question">How can a moving phone maintain good service without switching cells unnecessarily?</p>
    <p class="finding-summary"><strong>What we found:</strong> across the three frozen policies, aggregate throughput was <strong>8.86–9.99% higher</strong> and handovers per hour were <strong>36.08–53.00% fewer</strong> on the reserved Kathmandu-area cases, compared with the configured A3-style reference. The share of short completed stays increased. These are simulation findings.</p>
    <div class="research-perspectives">
      <div><h4>Wireless problem</h4><p>Serving-cell selection under changing signal conditions, mobility, and cell load. We assessed throughput alongside handovers, ping-pongs, weak service, and short cell stays.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Learning approach</h4><p>A graph-attention encoder and dueling Double DQN, compared with a configured A3-style controller under matched simulation conditions.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="research-bottom">
      <p class="research-scale">639 reserved Kathmandu-area cases<br>540 Pokhara route–layout–condition groups</p>
      <div class="inline-links">
          <a href="/research/">Study overview</a>
          <a href="/assets/documents/handover-study.pdf">Paper <span class="small-note">(PDF)</span></a>
          <a href="{{ profile.code }}">Code</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="interests research-directions" aria-label="Research interests and next questions">
  <div>
    <h2>Wireless communications</h2>
    <p>Mobility management, cellular network optimization, and 5G/6G networks.</p>
    <p class="interest-question">How do delayed or imperfect signal and load observations affect handover decisions?</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h2>Machine learning</h2>
    <p>Reinforcement learning, graph neural networks, and broader applications of AI/ML.</p>
    <p class="interest-question">When does graph structure help a learned policy, and does that benefit survive a change in network topology?</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="projects-heading">Projects &amp; practical work</h2><a href="/projects/">Project details and source</a></div>
  <div class="project-index">
    <article class="entry project-index-entry">
      <p class="project-type">Major project<span>2025–2026</span></p>
      <div>
      <h3><a href="/projects/#major-project">GNN-DQN Handover Optimization &amp; Load Balancing</a></h3>
      <p class="meta">One year, semesters 7–8 · Four-person team</p>
      <p>We explored graph-based reinforcement learning for LTE mobility and load balancing, then revised the work into a focused, two-author conference study of handover optimization.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry project-index-entry">
      <p class="project-type">Minor project<span>Semester 6 · 2025</span></p>
      <div>
      <h3><a href="/projects/#solvote">SolVote</a></h3>
      <p>A collaborative engineering prototype for voter registration, Solana-based token issuance, and electronic voting.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry project-index-entry">
      <p class="project-type">Side project<span>In development</span></p>
      <div>
      <h3><a href="/projects/#jamjamnepal">JAMJAMNEPAL — Tourism app</a></h3>
      <p>I’m developing a tourism application for domestic and international visitors to Nepal, building on a Go/Fiber and MongoDB foundation. AI integration is part of the planned development.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry project-index-entry">
      <p class="project-type">Networking labs<span>Hands-on coursework</span></p>
      <div>
      <h3><a href="/projects/#computer-networks">Computer networks: configuration &amp; packet analysis</a></h3>
      <p>Cisco Packet Tracer and Wireshark assignments covering IP configuration, connectivity checks between networks, DHCP/DNS simulation, and packet capture and filtering.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry project-index-entry">
      <p class="project-type">Software project<span>Swift · macOS</span></p>
      <div>
      <h3><a href="/projects/#clipboard-history">Clipboard History for macOS</a></h3>
      <p>A native menu-bar application for searching and reusing locally stored text clips, with keyboard shortcuts and no server requirement.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="experience-heading">Telecommunications experience</h2></div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <article class="entry">
      <div class="date-line"><h3>Nepal Telecom (NTC)</h3><span class="date">12 Jan – 27 Mar 2026</span></div>
      <p class="meta">Engineering Intern · Pokhara, Nepal</p>
      <p>Participated in handover and load-balancing activities, with exposure to GSM/LTE network planning, operation, optimization, and maintenance.</p>
      <p>The internship gave me practical context for the questions we were studying in our final-year project: how cellular networks operate, how mobility affects service, and what it means to optimize a network beyond a simulation.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="education-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="education-heading">Education</h2></div>
  <div class="section-body">
    {% for education in profile.education %}
    <article class="entry education-entry">
      <div class="date-line"><h3>{{ education.heading }}</h3>{% if education.period %}<span class="date">{{ education.period }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
      {% if education.institutionNote %}<p class="meta">{{ education.institutionNote }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if education.qualification %}<p>{{ education.qualification }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if education.result %}<p class="education-result"><strong>{{ education.result }}</strong></p>{% endif %}
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
    <p class="small-note qualification-note">Nepal Engineering Council engineering licensing examination passed.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="courses-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="courses-heading">Continuing to learn</h2><p>Alongside projects and research</p></div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <ul class="course-list course-list-home">
      {% for course in profile.courses %}{% if loop.index <= 2 %}
      <li><a href="{{ course.url }}">{{ course.title }}</a><span class="meta">{{ course.issuer }} · Coursera · {{ course.date }}</span></li>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="inline-links"><a href="/cv/#courses">All course credentials</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section contact-section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="contact-heading">Graduate research</h2></div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>I’m seeking a funded, research-based master’s or PhD opportunity for Fall 2027. I’m particularly interested in groups studying wireless network optimization, learning-based control, or reliable applied ML.</p>
    <p>I can contribute experience in Python/PyTorch implementation, simulation evaluation, and analysis, while developing deeper expertise through close research collaboration.</p>
    <p><a href="mailto:{{ profile.email }}">{{ profile.email }}</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
